## Built-in agent skills

Both built-in skills are shipped in `apps/server/src/agents/defaultSkills.ts`
and written into every agent home as `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.

### no-ai-slop

Adapted from **no-ai-slop** by Peter Yang — https://github.com/petergyang/no-ai-slop
Copyright (c) Peter Yang. Licensed under the MIT License.

Adapted: the upstream skill edits a draft the user pastes in. Taut's version is
scoped to the agent's own chat output (channel messages, thread replies, DMs,
task summaries) and explicitly does not apply to code, commits, PR descriptions
or files on disk.

### humanizer

**humanizer** v3.0.0 by blader — https://github.com/blader/humanizer
Copyright (c) blader. Licensed under the MIT License.

The body is included verbatim; only the frontmatter `description` is replaced,
to route on Taut chat messages rather than on a pasted draft.

The patterns in that skill derive from Wikipedia's "Signs of AI writing"
(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Signs_of_AI_writing), maintained by
WikiProject AI Cleanup, available under CC BY-SA 4.0.

